inely chopped\n* 1 ½ [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n* 2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]] [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Pound|pounds]] ice\n* 4 thick-cut [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]] rib chops\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] black [[Cookbook:Peppercorn|peppercorns]], cracked\n* 1 tablespoon smoked [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n* 1 tablespoon ancho [[Cookbook:Chiles|chile]] powder\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine honey, salt, vinegar, rosemary, thyme, cayenne pepper, and minced garlic in a plastic zip-top bag. Add ice, and shake the bag until ice is mostly melted and mixture has cooled down.\n#Insert pork chops into the bag, and refrigerate for 1–2 hours.\n#Combine cracked peppercorns, paprika, and chili powder.\n#Take the pork out of the mixture and pat dry with [[Cookbook:Paper Towel|paper towels]]. Discard remaining marinade.\n#Rub pepper mixture on both sides of each pork chop.\n#Quickly grease a high-heat [[Cookbook:Grill|grill]] with a flame-resistant towel soaked in oil and tied with twine.\n#[[Cookbook:Grilling|Grill]] pork chops, covered, 2 minutes. Rotate 90 degrees, and cook for another 2 minutes. Flip and repeat this process on the other side.\n#Move to a plate and let rest, uncovered, for 5 minutes. Serve warm.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using pork chop]]\n[[Category:Grilled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ancho chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using paprika]]\n[[Category:Recipes using honey]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Grilled Pork Chops","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup salt","sourceText":"1 cup salt","amountText":"1 cup salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"¾ cup honey","sourceText":"¾ cup honey","amountText":"¾ cup honey","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"